**Word Count Program in C++**
================================

This program reads a text file line by line and counts the number of occurrences of a specific word in the file.

### Program Code

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <fstream>
#include <sstream>
#include <string>
#include <map>

// Function to count the occurrences of a word in a line
int countWord(const std::string& line, const std::string& word) {
    int count = 0;
    std::istringstream iss(line);
    std::string token;
    while (iss >> token) {
        if (token == word) {
            count++;
        }
    }
    return count;
}

// Function to count the occurrences of a word in a file
int countWordInFile(const std::string& filename, const std::string& word) {
    int count = 0;
    std::ifstream file(filename);
    if (!file.is_open()) {
        std::cerr << "Error: Unable to open file " << filename << std::endl;
        return -1;
    }
    std::string line;
    while (std::getline(file, line)) {
        count += countWord(line, word);
    }
    file.close();
    return count;
}

int main() {
    std::string filename, word;
    std::cout << "Enter the filename: ";
    std::cin >> filename;
    std::cout << "Enter the word to search for: ";
    std::cin >> word;

    int count = countWordInFile(filename, word);
    if (count!= -1) {
        std::cout << "The word '" << word << "' appears " << count << " times in the file." << std::endl;
    }

    return 0;
}
```

### Explanation

This program consists of two main functions: `countWord` and `countWordInFile`. The `countWord` function takes a line of text and a word as input and returns the number of occurrences of the word in the line. The `countWordInFile` function takes a filename and a word as input and returns the total number of occurrences of the word in the file.

The `countWord` function uses a `std::istringstream` to split the line into individual words and then checks each word to see if it matches the target word.

The `countWordInFile` function opens the specified file, reads it line by line, and calls `countWord` for each line
